    "schema_diff_summary": "fuzzy.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only the letter check in digit_hump. Use is_alphabetic instead of is_ascii_alphabetic. Keep previous.is_numeric(). Keep the one && condition. Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch camel_bonus, boundary_bonus, or fuzzy_match. The existing tests a_digit_hump_adds_eight and a_fullwidth_digit_hump_adds_eight stay green. Do not rewrite their assertions. The test a_unicode_letter_after_a_digit_adds_eight uses fuzzy_match of e acute and the text 2 then capital E acute. The score is 24. The positions are 1. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
